    "created_at": "2018-09-29T03:10:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-29T03:17:53Z",
    "body": "Update: we've found that any _parent_ having `draggable` attribute will cause problems for child nodes that have `contenteditable`, with the exception of Chrome. Chrome does (imo) the right thing in that it allows the child to be `contenteditable` while the parent is `draggable`.\r\n\r\nFirefox gets close by allowing you to get a cursor but won't allow you to position the cursor on click (arrow keys & typing work however).\r\n\r\nSafari doesn't work at all. If the parent is `draggable` the child's `contenteditable` is completely clobbered. Impossible to get a cursor.\r\nUpdate: [jsfiddle](http://jsfiddle.net/4rdpV/57/) and [stackoverflow question](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6399131/html5-draggable-and-contenteditable-not-working-together)",
